From 7d892e9fee28346b90877126ae8fa42c97267cc8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Flopster101 <nahuelgomez329@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 15 May 2026 23:39:24 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] minuitwrp: graphics: Implement fix for color swap on
 Exynos fbdev

This is for Exynos devices where the kernel incorrectly reports a BGRA
pixel format, but actually requires RGBA in hardware.

It forces the internal surface format to BGRA_8888 while keeping the
system-wide RECOVERY_ABGR (assumming a pre-set ABGR_8888 pixel format
in BoardConfig). This trickery ensures Pixelflinger writes Red to byte 0.

TW_EXYNOS_FBDEV_COLOR_SWAP := true

Signed-off-by: Flopster101 <nahuelgomez329@gmail.com>
---
 .../images/Default/About/maintainer.png       | Bin 2353 -> 52846 bytes
 minuitwrp/graphics_fbdev.cpp                  |   5 +++++
 minuitwrp/libminuitwrp_defaults.go            |   4 ++++
 minuitwrp/resources.cpp                       |   3 +++
 4 files changed, 12 insertions(+)

